From 0ed9d3214716fe3b1d348130711de111cc6b0379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:44:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] anv/bvh: batch the scratch initializations of a build
 call in one dispatch

The IR header of every build (write_buffer_cp), the morton sort and
H-PLOC fills and the refit arrival counters were one blorp op each: a
compute dispatch with its own state, plus a texture cache invalidation
for every header copy. Cyberpunk rebuilds ~50 small BLAS per frame, so
~220 serialized blorp ops (~0.5 ms) ran before/between the first build
stages, and ~30 more before each refit.

Record them while vk_cmd_build_acceleration_structures() runs and execute
them all in one init.comp dispatch at the next flush_buffer_write_cp().
The common code now also calls flush_buffer_write_cp() after the scratch
fills.

tlascheck (TC_BLAS=51 TC_REFIT=141, clock pinned at 2850 MHz by load):
refit of 141 BLAS 1.139 -> 0.792 ms, rebuild of 51 BLAS 0.710 -> 0.569 ms,
0 wrong rays; rtcheck, ascopy and overrun clean.

ANV_BVH_BLORP_INIT=1 restores the blorp path for A/B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit dd6b5765fa1c24ad97d7d7ec04e86833567d82d3)
(cherry picked from commit c6d3d061ab6a3097e3f76bbec8d70c0390be2bad)
